Pack an export held in memory, and build for wasm32 (susz 0.1.4)

`pack::pack_to_vec` and `pack_file` only read from a path, and file
round trips through WASI's /tmp do not work under wasmfuzz.
`pack::pack_bytes_to_vec` packs a byte slice as `pack_to_vec` packs a
file on one thread (`lines::read_bytes`: one chunk, a newline added after
a last line without one, as `read_file` does at EOF). The parallel reader
(`pack::par`) uses std::os::unix::fs::FileExt and is gated to unix; with
one thread it is not used anyway.
Upstream: none (no issues at jasisz/susz; PRs #1-#5 are the author's own, checked 2026-11-22).

